<title>PERU: Peru's June mined iron output falls 1.6 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's June mined iron output falls 1.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's iron output fell 1.6 percent to 228,000 tonnes in June from the same month last year, according to preliminary figures released Thursday by Energy and Mines Ministry.</p>
<p>Iron output fell 19 percent overall in the first half of the year to 1.393 million tonnes from the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Peru's only iron miner is Chinese-owned Shougang Hierro Peru S.A, a former state-owned firm privatized in November 1992.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
